  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1107 AM CDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nBehind the front on Tuesday, temperatures and resultant heat \nindices take a dip back toward normal. Keep in mind that it's \nstill mid August, so \"normal\" is still hot, around 90 degrees. \nThis relief will be short-lived due to a warm front lifting across\nthe state on Wednesday, bringing us right back up to borderline \nHeat Advisory criteria. It's too early to make that call right \nnow, but we may just skirt by without heat headlines on Wednesday.\nThe majority of the warm front's impact will be felt over West \nTennessee with heat indices around 105 toward the TN River, but \nit will be close.\n\nThe pattern finally starts to mediate back toward climatological \nnormals at the end of the week. By Thursday, zonal flow aloft will\nhelp send heat and humidity well below headline thresholds. By \nFriday, expect heat indices below 100 degrees areawide for the \nfirst time in over a week. This cooler trend continues through \nnext weekend.",
